  "title": "IEEE 802.15.4: Fix ccm_cbc_mac stack buffer underflow",
  "description": "## IEEE 802.15.4: Fix ccm_cbc_mac stack buffer underflow\n\n### Problem\n\nCommit d6049d90d7 (\"dissectors: more cppcheck errors\") changed two\n`memset` calls in `ccm_cbc_mac()` in `packet-ieee802154.c`, introducing\na stack buffer underflow that crashes OSCORE decryption (and any other\ncaller of `ccm_cbc_mac` with non-16-byte-aligned AAD/ciphertext).\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe commit made two changes per line — a style change (pointer\narithmetic `block+x` → array index `&block[x]`, which is what cppcheck\nwanted) AND an index change (which introduced the bugs):\n\n1. **Line 5670**: `block+a_len` → `&block[a_len-1]`\n   - Off-by-one: overwrites the last byte of AuthData with 0.\n   - Fix: `&block[a_len]` (keeps array-index style, correct index).\n\n2. **Line 5690**: `block+m_len` → `&block[a_len]`\n   - Wrong variable: `a_len` is negative after the AuthData loop\n     completes, causing a stack buffer underflow that corrupts the\n     cipher handle and segfaults inside `gcry_cipher_encrypt`.\n   - Fix: `&block[m_len]` (keeps array-index style, correct variable).\n\n### Reproduction\n\nOSCORE decryption with AES-CCM-16-64-128 and a 1-byte ciphertext\nresponse crashes with SIGSEGV:\n\n```\nEXC_BAD_ACCESS (SIGSEGV), KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS at 0xb8\n\nFrame 0: _gcry_cipher_encrypt\nFrame 1: gcry_cipher_encrypt\nFrame 2: ccm_cbc_mac              [packet-ieee802154.c:5696]\nFrame 3: oscore_decrypt_and_verify [packet-oscore.c:562]\nFrame 4: oscore_dissect           [packet-oscore.c:631]\nFrame 5: call_dissector_with_data [packet-coap.c:1280]\n```\n\n### Verification\n\n- **OSCORE**: Decryption succeeds after the fix. Inner CoAP decoded\n  correctly (POST request and 2.04 Changed response). Authentication\n  tags verified.\n- **IEEE 802.15.4**: Sample capture (`ieee802154-association-data`)\n  processes without regression (13 packets).\n- **ZigBee**: Sample capture (`zigbee-join-authenticate`) with CCM*\n  network security processes without regression (54 packets, 28\n  security-level entries decoded).\n- **Build**: Compiles clean with no warnings.\n- **cppcheck**: No new warnings introduced. The array-index style\n  (`&block[x]`) that the original commit intended is preserved; only\n  the incorrect indices are corrected.\n\n### What This Fix Does NOT Revert\n\nCommit d6049d90d7 made other correct changes in the same file\n(`memcpy` for key assignment at lines 1976/1984, `ieee_hints` null\ncheck removal at lines 2871-2885). Those are **preserved** — this MR\nonly reverts the two buggy `memset` lines.\n\nFixup d6049d90d7\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (Claude)",
