      "title": "IEEE 802.15.4: Fix ccm_cbc_mac stack buffer underflow",
      "message": "IEEE 802.15.4: Fix ccm_cbc_mac stack buffer underflow\n\nCommit d6049d90d7 (\"dissectors: more cppcheck errors\") changed two\nmemset calls in ccm_cbc_mac() in packet-ieee802154.c, introducing a\nstack buffer underflow that crashes OSCORE decryption (and any other\ncaller of ccm_cbc_mac with non-16-byte-aligned AAD/ciphertext).\n\n1. Line 5670: &block[a_len-1] overwrites the last byte of AuthData\n   with 0 (off-by-one). Restore &block[a_len].\n\n2. Line 5690: &block[a_len] uses a_len, which is negative after the\n   AuthData loop completes, causing a stack buffer underflow that\n   corrupts the cipher handle and segfaults inside gcry_cipher_encrypt.\n   Restore &block[m_len] (the message length, which is the correct\n   variable for the message-padding branch).\n\nReproduced: OSCORE decryption with AES-CCM-16-64-128 and a 1-byte\nciphertext response crashes with SIGSEGV in gcry_cipher_encrypt\ncalled from ccm_cbc_mac (packet-ieee802154.c:5696).\n\nVerified: OSCORE decryption succeeds after the fix (inner CoAP\ndecoded correctly). IEEE 802.15.4 and ZigBee captures with CCM*\nsecurity process without regression.\n\nFixup d6049d90d7\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (Claude)\n",
